WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.735
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.604
I love that energy.
Thank you so much.

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.638
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.040
Nice to see you.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.909
Guys, today is Earth Day.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.944
Happy Earth Day!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:14.079
Everyone's in the spirit.
This morning at 7-Eleven,

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:16.949
I saw a rat drinking a Big Gulp
with a metal straw.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.786
-Aww.
-Yes -- So, yes.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.554
A lot of stores
celebrated Earth Day.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.391
H&amp;M added a section
for sustainable items.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.692
Lowe's offered a free
Garden-to-Go kit,

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:29.062
and Subway recycled
last week's tuna.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.330
-Oh.
-So, yeah, I thought that was --

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.499
I'm kidding around, but
protecting the Earth is serious.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:35.501
I mean, can you believe
that in 1999,

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.637
we had nearly 50
Rainforest Cafes,

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.405
and now we're down to almost 20?

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:41.774
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:45.511
Think about it.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:47.246
That's right.
Today was all about the planet,

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:48.380
and at the White House,

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.517
President Biden
hosted 40 world leaders

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:53.019
for a virtual
climate change summit.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:56.289
The tone of the summit
was that we're all responsible.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.258
But you know Costa Rica was
looking at the U.S. and China

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.993
like, "Yeah.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:02.895
This is all our fault, right?
Yeah, we're --

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.797
We're all to blame. Yeah.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:06.533
Huh. Yeah."

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:09.001
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:10.403
Now, of course,
with any virtual event,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.972
you're going to have some
technical glitches, right?

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.874
But I didn't think
it'd be quite this bad.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.109
Take a look at what happened.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.211
-[ Echoing ] Good morning
to all our colleagues --

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.679
all our colleagues
around the world,

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:22.481
the world leaders taking part
in the summit, I thank you.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:24.283
-It's now my honor to call on

00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:26.686
His Excellency, The Secretary
General of the United Nations,

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.021
António Guterres.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.689
[ No audio ]

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.823
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.424
I now call upon
the Prime Minister

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:34.827
of the Republic of India,
His Excellency Narendra Modi.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.162
-President Biden...

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.865
[ Phone dialing ]

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:41.400
...my fellow citizens.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.435
[ Phone dialing ]

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.903
-The floor is now to

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:47.039
the President of the Russian
Federation, Mr. Vladimir Putin.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.942
Mr. President.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.678
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.817
-What?

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:58.918
[ Applause ]

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.854
Looking.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.757
Somehow we just flew
a helicopter on Mars,

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.760
but we still can't get
a Zoom meeting to work.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.395
Next time, every leader
will be required

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.564
to have at least
one grandchild present.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.799
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.067
It is funny that we were
watching Putin,

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.501
and he didn't know
he was on-camera,

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.670
'cause usually,
it's the other way around.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.005
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.039
Yeah.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.107
Even --

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:23.676
-That was a good one.
That was good.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.379
-At one point, Britain's Prime
Minister, Boris Johnson, spoke,

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:29.615
and he used a pretty interesting
phrase to get his point across.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:30.649
Listen to this.

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:32.285
-This is not all about

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:36.623
some expensive, politically
correct green act

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:40.493
of -- of -- of bunny-hugging

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.495
or however you want to put it.

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:43.729
There's nothing wrong
with bunny-hugging,

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:46.232
but you -- you know
what I'm driving at.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.267
-No.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.136
We have no idea
what you're driving at.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:51.204
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.472
At first, people were like, "Oh,

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:55.441
is bunny-hugging a British
version of tree-hugging?"

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.410
British people were like,
"No, he's just weird.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.945
I've never heard that term."

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:01.548
That's right, leaders
from all over the world

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:03.549
met to discuss
climate change over Zoom,

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.753
and some even released joint
statements with President Biden.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:07.920
Check these out.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.256
After French President
Emanuel Macron said,

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:13.392
"If we want to decrease our
carbon footprint, we must..."

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:14.693
Biden jumped in and said,

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:17.129
"Take a page
out of my old friend's book.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:19.198
His name was Shoeless Gus.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.600
He used to walk across
a gravel parking lot

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.169
just to prove a point.

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:26.139
He ran off with a flapper girl
from Cheyenne.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:28.841
Now they sell tire swings
for a living."

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:30.543
[ Applause ]

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:32.378
I --
-Wow.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.779
-I don't really see
how that's relevant,

00:03:33.779 --> 00:03:36.048
but let's check out
another joint statement.

00:03:36.048 --> 00:03:38.351
After German Chancellor
Angela Merkel said,

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:42.121
"We can conserve the amount of
available water we have by..."

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.690
Biden said, "Roundin' up
all the neighborhood boys

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.892
and washin' ourselves off
in the creek

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:50.496
behind Old Man MacGafferty's
tool shed.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.798
Just as good as a real shower,
and you get to eat

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:56.269
as many tadpole eggs
as you can fit in your mouth."

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:58.071
-Wait, what?

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:00.573
-What?

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.208
Like, why do they keep
letting him talk?

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.475
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:03.475 --> 00:04:05.478
Let's check out one more.
-Alright, let's see it.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.580
-After British Prime Minister
Boris Johnson said,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.748
"Fighting climate change

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.117
will create millions of jobs,
such as..."

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:15.555
Biden said, "Root beer barbers
and professional whistlers.

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:19.258
I used to know a pair of twins
who could whistle like a teapot.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:23.829
Their parents named 'em both
Ralph to make things easy.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.531
One of 'em
got struck by lightning,

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.599
and after that, anytime
he walked past a jukebox,

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:29.201
it just started playing."

00:04:29.201 --> 00:04:30.236
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.471
-Wow.
-Ralph and Ralph?

00:04:32.471 --> 00:04:33.639
I don't know.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:34.673
-They sound like
joint statements.

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.109
-I don't know, man.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.078
More news from Washington.
After the White House presented

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:41.948
its $2.3 trillion
infrastructure plan,

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.450
Republicans have responded
with their own version

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.553
that's only worth $568 billion.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.089
Yeah, Republicans want all these
repairs done on the cheap,

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:53.092
which is why they're calling
the bill "Operation Flex Seal."

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.793
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:56.796
Biden has so much
on his plate -- infrastructure,

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.498
construction, police reform,
military spending --

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:01.901
right now, his to-do list
looks like the Village People.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.504
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.107
This is pretty incredible.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:11.443
I saw that Amazon is testing out
a new way to pay at Whole Foods.

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:12.712
Take a look at this.

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:15.481
-Paying for groceries
with a swipe of your hand.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.016
That could be coming soon
to Whole Foods stores near you.

00:05:18.016 --> 00:05:19.852
It allows shoppers
to pay for items

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:23.189
by placing their palm
over the scanning device.

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.091
-Here's how it works. You hover
your hand over the reader,

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:26.959
then the cashier tells you to
stay still,

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:30.063
then move it slightly,
then move it slightly again,

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:32.031
and then you get frustrated
and pay with your credit card.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.800
-Wow. Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.933
-Whatever. I think it's fun.

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:38.037
I always wanted to buy plums
like I'm a Jedi.

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.505
-Beep!

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.974
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.108
-That's pretty good, right?

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:44.977
-Beep. Yeah, that's
a pretty good Jedi.

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.412
-Like, it's
the move back that's --

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.980
-The move back
is what sells it. Yeah.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.515
That's just a guy.

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:50.917
-Yeah.
-That's a Jedi.

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:52.118
-Thank you.

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:53.185
-Especially with the flourish.

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:55.754
-Are they making another
"Star Wars" film?

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:58.291
-I bet they -- Oh. You could --

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:01.460
-I added a little mustard
on that last one.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.494
You want me to do it
one more time?

00:06:02.494 --> 00:06:03.596
-Do it one more time.
-Mr. Lucas?

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:04.930
Okay.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.532
Step to the left. Yeah. More?

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:07.566
-More?
-More?

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:08.701
-How far?
-Okay, perfect.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.736
This is good?
-Do I have a car?

00:06:09.736 --> 00:06:11.370
-Okay.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.404
Thank you.

00:06:12.404 --> 00:06:16.242
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:18.478
An Academy Award?

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:20.712
Oh, it's not --
My name's not on it.

00:06:20.712 --> 00:06:21.781
Well, this is interesting.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.282
Scientists are
developing technology

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:26.652
that lets them add product
placement in classic films.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.087
Yeah.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:30.356
We actually got our hands on the
first few clips they produced.

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:33.459
Now, watch closely, because
the ads are incredibly subtle.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:34.493
Roll it.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:36.963
-It's December 1941
in Casablanca.

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.998
What time is it in New York?

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.532
-What?

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:41.901
My watch stopped.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.536
-Bet they're asleep in New York.

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:46.072
[ Apes screeching, growling ]

00:06:48.273 --> 00:06:49.542
-Say again, please?

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.544
-Houston, we have a --
-Tide Pod.

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.145
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.145 --> 00:06:55.214
[ Applause ]

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:01.286
-Oh, this isn't good.
McCormick said

00:07:01.286 --> 00:07:03.356
that they've had a difficult
time keeping up with demand

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:06.091
for Old Bay Seasoning
during the pandemic.

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:08.394
Can't really imagine why,
which brings us to a new segment

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:11.197
we like to call
"Tariq's Teachable Moment."

00:07:11.263 --> 00:07:13.599
-"Tariq's Teachable Moment."

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:15.767
[ Applause ]

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:18.437
-Thanks, Jimmy. I think
I can shine a light on this.

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:21.507
You see, when Black people cook,

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.809
we enjoy this thing
that you might have heard of.

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:25.778
It's called flavor.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:26.812
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:29.114
Flavor is what happens to a meal

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:32.418
when you add more to it
than just salt or pepper.

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.453
-I don't know. That sounds
spicy.

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:35.754
-It can be.

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:39.825
In Black homes, spice racks
are like guard dogs --

00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:43.129
robust, loud, integral parts
of the family unit.

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:47.133
Meanwhile, your spice rack
is more like a lap dog --

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:51.336
small, decorative,
but ultimately useless.

00:07:51.336 --> 00:07:54.940
So, when the pandemic hit
and restaurants closed,

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:58.110
Black people treated Old Bay
like it was toilet paper

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:00.846
and bought enough
to fill a bunker.

00:08:00.846 --> 00:08:03.849
-Okay, well, how much seasoning
should I use?

00:08:03.849 --> 00:08:06.752
-A great start would be
more than zero.

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.187
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:11.224
Just do what I do.
Ignore the recipe

00:08:11.224 --> 00:08:15.394
and sprinkle it on a little
longer than you usually would.

00:08:15.394 --> 00:08:17.830
Like this.

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:25.338
[ Laughter ]

00:08:27.539 --> 00:08:29.442
-Okay, this seems like a lot.

00:08:29.442 --> 00:08:31.410
-It is. That's the point, Jimmy.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.413
And look, if you don't
understand yet, that's okay.

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:37.016
Just give it a minute
to marinate.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.417
[ Ding! ]

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:39.652
[ Applause ]

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:43.055
-"Tariq's Teachable Moment."

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:44.590
-Tariq Trotter, everybody.
Tariq Trotter.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.425
I learned a lot.
Thank you, Tariq.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:49.294
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:49.294 --> 00:08:52.031
And finally, a woman in North
Carolina was shopping at Target

00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:55.134
when she found a surprise
on the shelf. Watch this.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:57.769
-Aah.
-This is not something

00:08:57.769 --> 00:09:00.305
you typically find
on the shelves in Target --

00:09:00.305 --> 00:09:01.607
a black rat snake

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:05.177
slithering through the cans
of Bush's Baked Beans.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:06.845
-Ooh.
-Manager came on the PA system

00:09:06.845 --> 00:09:10.549
and was like, "Oh, hell no,
in Aisle 5. Oh, hell no."

00:09:10.549 --> 00:09:13.752
Joining us in-studio,
one of our absolute favorites.

00:09:13.752 --> 00:09:15.253
-A delight.
-The guy is a gem.

00:09:15.253 --> 00:09:18.291
He stars in the Showtime series
"City on a Hill."

00:09:18.291 --> 00:09:20.593
Kevin Bacon is here!
-Yeah! Come on!

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:22.661
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:22.661 --> 00:09:24.162
-The best.

00:09:24.162 --> 00:09:27.098
Plus, she's a four-time
Olympic gold medal gymnast,

00:09:27.098 --> 00:09:28.867
Simone Biles is here.

00:09:28.867 --> 00:09:31.370
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:35.974
And we got great music
from Ritt Momney, everybody!

00:09:35.974 --> 00:09:38.144
Ritt Momney.
-Ritt. Ritt.

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:40.446
-Ritt Momney. That's right.

00:09:40.446 --> 00:09:43.082
And later, we're going to have
all-new "Tonight Show" Hashtags,

00:09:43.082 --> 00:09:45.150
as well. Yeah.
-Ooh.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.719
-And we're going to do something
fun with Kevin Bacon.

00:09:47.719 --> 00:09:48.754
-Oh!

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:50.056
-Something musical perhaps.

00:09:50.056 --> 00:09:52.158
-Perhaps!

00:09:52.158 --> 00:09:53.325
More Jedi --

00:09:53.325 --> 00:09:54.593
-A sketch per--

00:09:54.593 --> 00:09:55.994
I retired
from the Jedi business.

00:09:55.994 --> 00:09:58.631
-Are you serious? What happened?
-It was too hard on my arm.

00:09:58.631 --> 00:10:01.300
Everywhere I went, everyone
was like, "Do the Jedi thing."

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.801
-Oh.
-Leave me alone.

00:10:02.801 --> 00:10:04.936
I'm just a normal person.
-Oh, it was like a curse.

00:10:04.936 --> 00:10:08.306
-Yeah, I was cursed
by my own Jedi techniques.

00:10:08.306 --> 00:10:10.275
And I couldn't go shopping.
I couldn't go anywhere.

00:10:10.275 --> 00:10:11.911
It was a nightmare.
Can you imagine my life?

00:10:11.911 --> 00:10:13.712
-No, I can't imagine,
'cause, I mean --

00:10:13.712 --> 00:10:17.816
-"Do the Jedi thing! Do it!
Do it now! Do it now!"

00:10:17.816 --> 00:10:19.217
-You're with your family.

00:10:19.217 --> 00:10:21.353
-Yeah, my kids are around.
-And you told me the one time,

00:10:21.353 --> 00:10:22.955
you were about to have
emergency surgery,

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:25.057
and the doctor made you do it
before you had the surgery.

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:30.896
-Yeah, I'm basically on the
death bed, whatever it is, yeah.

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:32.732
-Death bed, sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.732 --> 00:10:34.600
-Got tubes all over the place.
-Yeah.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.168
-My life turned into
a complete --

00:10:36.168 --> 00:10:38.437
No one remembered that I hosted
"The Tonight Show" or anything.

00:10:38.437 --> 00:10:39.605
-They just remembered you
from the --

00:10:39.605 --> 00:10:41.507
Well, it was so good,
I can't blame them.

00:10:41.507 --> 00:10:43.943
-Well, they cut it out
of the Blu-ray.

00:10:43.943 --> 00:10:45.077
[ Laughter ]

00:10:45.077 --> 00:10:47.045
-Are you serious?
-Yeah.

00:10:47.045 --> 00:10:49.314
-The whole Jedi thing
is gone from the Blu-ray?

00:10:49.314 --> 00:10:51.016
-Well, when you get the Blu--

00:10:51.016 --> 00:10:52.584
-What about the Laser--
Is it on the LaserDisc?

00:10:52.584 --> 00:10:54.320
-No, they took it
out of the LaserDisc, as well.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.955
-Oh, my God.
-And the Blu-ray.

00:10:55.955 --> 00:10:59.057
And I was like,
"Get me George Lucas on Line 2.

00:10:59.057 --> 00:11:01.160
Oh -- Get me George Lucas
on Line 2."

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:03.028
Then I picked up the phone,
pressed Line 2.

00:11:03.028 --> 00:11:04.563
-Right.

00:11:09.001 --> 00:11:11.503
-Hello?

00:11:11.503 --> 00:11:13.538
-Uh, hello, Jimmy?

00:11:13.538 --> 00:11:14.974
-Is this George Lucas?

00:11:14.974 --> 00:11:17.809
-Uh, no. This is, uh, Gary,
his assistant.

00:11:17.809 --> 00:11:19.912
George is busy.

00:11:19.912 --> 00:11:21.246
-The assistant's assistant?

00:11:21.246 --> 00:11:23.249
-Yeah, I'm the fifth assistant.

00:11:23.249 --> 00:11:25.250
-Fifth -- George Lucas
has five assistants?

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.986
-No, he has 12 assistants.
-Sorry, I --

00:11:26.986 --> 00:11:28.253
-Some of them are
sick with COVID.

00:11:28.253 --> 00:11:29.922
-I apolog-- I understand.

00:11:29.922 --> 00:11:31.123
I don't work there, so...
-Pandemic going on.

00:11:31.123 --> 00:11:32.391
-I apologize.

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.426
Could you let George know
I'm a little upset.

00:11:34.426 --> 00:11:35.794
-About?

00:11:35.794 --> 00:11:39.298
-I was in the new
"Star Wars" film.

00:11:39.298 --> 00:11:41.567
-Okay.
-And I was the --

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:44.403
[ Laughter ]

00:11:44.403 --> 00:11:46.572
That's not why I was upset.
-Oh, okay.

00:11:46.572 --> 00:11:49.208
Sorry. A lot of people are
complaining about it.

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:52.111
-No, I would never
complain about being --

00:11:52.111 --> 00:11:55.080
But it's just, I did a Jedi -- I
played a Jedi, did a Jedi move.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.348
-Oh, yeah.

00:11:56.348 --> 00:11:58.283
-The hand move?
-Loved it.

00:11:58.283 --> 00:12:00.852
-You remember it?
-Who doesn't?

00:12:00.852 --> 00:12:02.587
-[ Scoffs ] Apparently,
George didn't like it.

00:12:02.587 --> 00:12:04.489
He cut it out of the --
-No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no,

00:12:04.489 --> 00:12:06.258
no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no.

00:12:06.258 --> 00:12:08.593
-Please, I don't like your tone.
-He loved it so much.

00:12:08.593 --> 00:12:09.862
-Oh.

00:12:09.862 --> 00:12:13.232
-It made the rest of the movie
look like garbage.

00:12:13.232 --> 00:12:14.866
He had no choice
but to take it out.

00:12:14.866 --> 00:12:16.902
The genius of that moment

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:19.705
made the rest of the film
look like...

00:12:19.705 --> 00:12:21.273
-Garbage.
-...a dog vomited

00:12:21.273 --> 00:12:23.575
on its own poop.
-Oh.

00:12:23.575 --> 00:12:24.910
-That's a bad image.
-Gary, I thank you so much.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.579
I apologize that
I put you in a bad mood,

00:12:27.579 --> 00:12:29.614
but you changed my day,
and thank you so much

00:12:29.614 --> 00:12:31.717
for taking me --
-One more thing, just, if I may?

00:12:31.717 --> 00:12:32.951
-Sure.
-I know I'm over the phone,

00:12:32.951 --> 00:12:35.154
but...could you do it for me?

00:12:35.154 --> 00:12:37.523
[ Laughter ]

00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:49.235
Oh, my God.

00:12:49.235 --> 00:12:50.836
-You take care, buddy.
-Thank you so much.

00:12:50.836 --> 00:12:52.070
-Be well. Be well.

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:53.105
♪♪

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:54.240
Nice guy.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:56.208
Really nice guy.

00:12:56.208 --> 00:12:57.610
And thanks to George Lucas.

